{% comment %}
  A token that changes whenever the site is rebuilt, for appending to the
  stylesheet and script URLs.

  Those two are served as one fixed filename each with a ten-minute freshness
  window, so without this a reader can be handed HTML from the new build and
  keep serving themselves CSS and JS from the old one. Everything that depends
  on the two agreeing -- the bilingual rules and the nav script most visibly --
  is broken for exactly as long as that lasts.

  The commit SHA is the honest token on GitHub Pages: it changes when, and only
  when, the built output can have changed. Locally that variable is empty, so
  the build timestamp stands in, which errs toward re-fetching rather than
  toward showing a preview stale assets.
{% endcomment %}
{% if site.github.build_revision %}
  {% assign asset_version = site.github.build_revision | slice: 0, 8 %}
{% else %}
  {% assign asset_version = site.time | date: '%s' %}
{% endif %}
